{
  "core_question": "What analyses must the hospital board conduct across clinical, legal, and financial domains to evaluate a private‑equity acquisition involving conversion to for‑profit status, sale‑leaseback of real estate, and a charitable foundation holding proceeds?",
  "rationale": "The transaction touches patient care operations (clinical), regulatory and tax compliance (legal), and valuation, financing, and cash‑flow implications (finance).",
  "routes": ["healthcare", "legal", "finance"],
  "sub_questions": {
    "healthcare": "What clinical considerations—including impact on staffing, quality metrics, accreditation status, patient safety, and continuity of care—should the board evaluate when a nonprofit community hospital converts to for‑profit ownership and enters a sale‑leaseback arrangement for its real estate?",
    "legal": "From a legal standpoint, what are the key regulatory, tax, licensing, fiduciary, and contractual issues the board must address in converting the operating entity from nonprofit to for‑profit, structuring a sale‑leaseback of hospital property, and establishing a charitable foundation that holds the proceeds of the transaction?",
    "finance": "What financial analyses—including valuation of the hospital assets and operations, lease terms and obligations, tax consequences for the nonprofit and for‑profit entities, impact on debt capacity, cash‑flow projections, and expected returns to the private‑equity sponsor—should the board review before approving this acquisition?"
  },
